   "title": "Pythagoras' Theorem & SOHCAHTOA",
   "content": "<p><strong>Pythagoras:</strong> \\(a^2 + b^2 = c^2\\) where \\(c\\) is the hypotenuse. To find a shorter side: \\(a^2 = c^2 - b^2\\).</p><p><strong>SOHCAHTOA:</strong></p><p>\\(\\sin\\theta = \\frac{\\text{Opp}}{\\text{Hyp}}\\), \\(\\cos\\theta = \\frac{\\text{Adj}}{\\text{Hyp}}\\), \\(\\tan\\theta = \\frac{\\text{Opp}}{\\text{Adj}}\\)</p><p>To find an angle: use the inverse function (e.g. \\(\\theta = \\sin^{-1}(\\frac{O}{H})\\)).</p>",
   "example": "<p><strong>Find the hypotenuse: sides 6 and 8.</strong></p><p>\\(c^2 = 6^2 + 8^2 = 36 + 64 = 100\\). \\(c = 10\\).</p>"
  },
